CRITICAL ROOT FINDING
---------------------
The old simple hypothesis "each tab length - electrode width must be > 0" is FALSE.

Define:
  Delta+    = positive tab length - positive electrode width
  Delta-    = negative tab length - negative electrode width
  Delta_avg = (Delta+ + Delta-) / 2

Runtime evidence:
  H01:  0 / +8       -> PASS
  H05: +9 /  0       -> PASS
  T01: +0.89 / -0.11 -> PASS
  H09:  0 / 0        -> E004
  H10: +0.10/+0.10   -> E004
  H11: +0.70/+0.70   -> PASS
  T02:  0/0          -> E004
  T03: +0.10/+0.10   -> E004
  T04: +0.70/+0.70   -> PASS
  T09: -4.11/-5.11   -> E004

Within tested H/T cases:
  Delta_avg <= 0.10 mm -> E004
  Delta_avg >= 0.39 mm -> PASS

This is an EMPIRICAL separator, not a claimed Siemens formula. Root construction is clearly coupled between electrodes / available end geometry rather than two independent direct extrusions.

STEP evidence shows generated tab/root geometry increases with combined available surplus and then saturates. T06-like +2/+2 mm surplus is already at the same practical generated end geometry as much larger T07/T08 cases. Use T06-like axial/root geometry as the next stable base.

